{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963430,"nonce":"ikff+8vw6Mi1yrClZggDqNYIKI0=","title":"awaiting a pending future never wakes once a window has opened","message":"With a winit window open on macOS (xwindow.hdll, even an invisible window), `ash.Future.await()` on a future that is still pending parks the main fiber and never returns, though a foreign thread settles the future. Without a window the same await returns, and with the window open polling `isReady()` between `Sys.sleep` calls sees the future settle.\n\nReproducer, with hlwgpu's xgpu.hdll and hlwgpu's xwindow.hdll (crates/hlwindow) beside the program:\n\n    var attributes = new window.WindowAttributes();\n    attributes.visible(false);\n    var w = window.Window.open(attributes);\n    var pending = new gpu.GpuInstance().requestAdapter(gpu.Power.HighPerformance);\n    trace(pending.await().name()); // never returns; without Window.open it prints the adapter\n\nxgpu's backend resolves the adapter from a `std::thread::spawn`ed thread through `hlp_future_resolve`. A sample of the hung process shows the main thread looping in `ash_std::fiber::park` (gc_safepoint, gc_set_blocking, pthread_cond_broadcast) and no other thread with work: the completion happened and its wake was lost. Opening the window initialises AppKit's NSApplication on the main thread first.","files":null}]}